{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"The next PR #652 rerun showed Mosquitto could not open the config file generated under a mode-700 mktemp directory; the earlier run also showed its shared PID path was unwritable.","decision":"Make each smoke-only config directory searchable and its config readable by the Mosquitto service account, and omit the PID file because these supervised foreground smoke processes do not need one.","impact":"Changed only Scripts/container-smoke.sh and Scripts/runner-smoke.sh. The processes still run foreground under the smoke shell and are cleaned up on exit. No application or dependency changes.","recurrence_control":"The scripts use per-run temporary configs, bounded connection probes, captured logs, and child cleanup. bash -n, make harness-test, and git diff --check pass; CI must verify the container-specific permission behavior.","rejected_alternatives":["Keep a private mode-700 config directory that the service account cannot traverse.","Retain a PID file whose target cannot be written by the runtime account."],"sources":[]}
